WEBVTT

NOTE
Transcribed from the narration in this video. Every figure the
speaker states matches the OECD time-use data behind this page.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.740
Hey, you want to see
how my day works?

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.080
Come, I'll walk you through it.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.660
I start with 10 hours and
40 minutes of personal care.

4
00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.380
Sleep, a bath, breakfast.

5
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.000
That's 25 minutes less than
the 35 country average.

6
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.160
We're efficient even at resting.

7
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.900
Then, I'm at work.

8
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.500
6 hours and 8 minutes
of paid work a day.

9
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.080
The most in the data.

10
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.520
That's 96 minutes above
the 35 country average.

11
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.420
There's a word for it here.

12
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.480
Ikigai?

13
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.620
Finding purpose in what you do.

14
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:32.420
Lunch?

15
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.940
A quick bowl of ramen between shifts.

16
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.420
Then back to it.

17
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.520
At home, I spend about
2 hours and 5 minutes

18
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.420
on unpaid work, the lowest
of the 35 countries.

19
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.960
But here's something important.

20
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.820
Japanese women carry
a much bigger share,

21
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.360
about 161 minutes
more per day than men.

22
00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.660
That's a conversation we're having.

23
00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:55.640
Leisure?

24
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.900
4 hours and 29 minutes.

25
00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.900
That's 19 minutes below average.

26
00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.900
But those moments feel earned.

27
00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:04.300
And I'll work until about 71.

28
00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:07.380
That's 5.6 years longer
than the average.

29
00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.340
Camille will have been
retired for a decade by then.

30
00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.112
That's my day in Japan.
